eometric series $0.1+0.11+0.121+0.133\\,1+⋯$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{0.11}{0.1} \\\\  & =1.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent  because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only series II converges." 13194139534533 true] [17592186293476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293477 13194139534533 true] [17592186293476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293478 13194139534533 true] [17592186293476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293479 13194139534533 true] [17592186293476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293480 13194139534533 true] [17592186293476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293481 13194139534533 true] [17592186293476 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534533 true] [17592186293476 1041 "selection" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293476 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293481 13194139534533 true] [17592186293476 1110 #uuid "cf9be666-3755-56fd-b7a4-bfdfe407b825" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293477 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293477 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534533 true] [17592186293477 1111 #uuid "1db5356e-50e1-59b3-bb3e-b2f75abf8053" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293478 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293478 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534533 true] [17592186293478 1111 #uuid "852359ed-8cf2-5bf5-a3f5-621916fc8cb4" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293479 1034 "I only" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293479 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534533 true] [17592186293479 1111 #uuid "c68a442b-2ecc-57ac-a851-f52e0b1bf81f" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293480 1034 "III only" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293480 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534533 true] [17592186293480 1111 #uuid "c59ce3d3-43c6-5524-8cd0-b01523e025ff" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293481 1034 "II only" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293481 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534533 true] [17592186293481 1111 #uuid "f398900c-0757-548b-931c-76d1a6a4dd7e" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293482 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293483 13194139534533 true] [17592186293482 1089 "q-124924" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293482 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534533 true] [17592186293482 1100 "For which values of $k$ does the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{10}^{kn-1}}{{100}^{n}}$ converge?" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293482 1113 #uuid "f3040a9b-f07a-5c90-9674-eff18efde317" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293482 1145 "First, we rewrite the series so that it's in the form ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }a{r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{10}^{kn-1}}{{100}^{n}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{10}^{kn}}{{100}^{n}\\cdot 10} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot {(\\frac{{10}^{k}}{100})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that this is a geometric series with a common ratio of $r=\\frac{{10}^{k}}{100}.$ \n\nFor the series to converge, we require $|r|<1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{{10}^{k}}{100}| & <1 \\\\ \\frac{{10}^{k}}{100} & <1 \\\\ {10}^{k} & <100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we could remove the absolute value bars because $\\frac{{10}^{k}}{100}$ is always positive.\n\nThe equation ${10}^{k}=100$ has the solution $k=2.$ Now, since ${10}^{k}$ increases as $k$ increases, the solution to ${10}^{k}<100$ must be $k<2.$" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293483 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293484 13194139534533 true] [17592186293483 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293485 13194139534533 true] [17592186293483 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293486 13194139534533 true] [17592186293483 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293487 13194139534533 true] [17592186293483 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293488 13194139534533 true] [17592186293483 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534533 true] [17592186293483 1041 "selection" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293483 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293487 13194139534533 true] [17592186293483 1110 #uuid "cb2a0ad3-7172-5af3-bbae-a6ab9da2e6ed" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293484 1034 "k>2" 13194139534533 true] [17592186293484 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13